This default was chosen because Hidook Site Builder is `"private": true`
commercial software (see `package.json`) sold as a hosted product, not a
published open-source project — a proprietary "all rights reserved" notice is
the standard default for a private commercial codebase absent an explicit
owner decision to open-source some or all of it. It has not been confirmed
by the product owner and does not itself determine the license terms under
which a *customer's own generated site* (the HTML/CSS/JS a customer
downloads via Export ZIP/HTML, built from their own content) may be used —
that is a separate product/legal decision the owner has not made either; see
`HANDOFF-docs.md`.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses:

- `bot/` — `grammy` (MIT) — see `bot/package-lock.json` for the resolved
  version and `node_modules/grammy/LICENSE` after `npm install`.
- Root — `playwright` (Apache-2.0), a devDependency used only for test/QA
  tooling, not shipped to customers.

The exact legal entity name, jurisdiction, and whether any part of this
codebase should be dual-licensed or open-sourced are owner decisions per
`VISION.md` §10 (Owner gates) and have not been made as of this writing —
do not treat the "Hidook" name above as a confirmed legal entity name; it is
the product's public brand name used elsewhere in this repository
(`README.md`, `PRODUCT.md`).
